/** @page v8releasenotesguide v8 Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section v8_build_compatibility Node.js Build Compatibility

    - GNU and Clang builds use Node's documented C++ aliasing setting for its inline V8 callbacks.
    - Documentation imports the packaged DataProvider and ConnectionProvider indexes and corrects
      stale reference targets and misplaced parameter documentation. Packaging can enable
      \c QORE_V8_STRICT_DOCS to fail documentation generation on warnings.

    @section v8_2_2 v8 Module Version 2.2
    - the time limits of TypeScript app calls and of \c ts-proxy child process startup take effect as documented:
      each call of an app's or action's function (such as an API, record or webhook function) fails after 30
      minutes by default, so long API and AI actions can complete, while a call that never answers no longer
      waits over 8 hours; change the limit with \c TypeScriptActionInterface::setCallTimeout() or the
      \c QORE_TYPESCRIPT_CALL_TIMEOUT_SECS environment variable (a number of seconds), and an app or action can
      set its own with \c io_timeout_secs.  Calls run in \c ts-proxy child processes get the same limit instead of
      failing after 90 seconds.  Event functions have no limit; event sources no longer stop after just over 8
      hours.  A new \c ts-proxy child process has 60 seconds to start by default (it had over 5 hours) and is
      terminated if it has not started by then; change this with \c JavaScriptProgramProxy::setStartupTimeout()
      or the \c QORE_TYPESCRIPT_PROXY_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_SECS environment variable
    - \c qore-app-schemas and \c qore-hubspot-schemas exit with the new status 69 when a schema source cannot be
      reached or does not answer (the connection failed or closed before the response was complete, no complete
      response arrived within 30 seconds, or the source answered HTTP 408, 429 or 5xx); the message names the URL, the
      error code or HTTP status and the \c Retry-After value that the source sent.  Any other HTTP status remains exit
      status 1; an update of several apps exits with 2 if any schema was refused, otherwise with the status that
      every failure has, and 1 for different ones.  Every schema download
      now opens a connection of its own, so a server closing a connection that an earlier download left open no
      longer fails the next download with \c "socket hang up"; nothing is retried
    - CI qualifies the HubSpot, Pipedrive and Trello schema documents that it pins by SHA-256 from a private mirror
      instead of downloading them from the upstream services; every document is checked against its own pin, and a
      daily scheduled check compares the upstream documents with the pins and runs the update commands against the
      upstream services
    - fixed creating @ref V8::JavaScriptProgram "JavaScriptProgram" and @ref V8::TypeScriptProgram
      "TypeScriptProgram" objects in multiple threads at the same time: a program could run the source of another
      program created at the same time, and on Alpine Linux (musl) the process could crash later at random, for
      example with a segmentation fault or <tt>Check failed: 0 == munmap(address, size)</tt>; programs no longer
      set the \c _qore_v8_source, \c _qore_v8_filename and \c _qore_v8_dirname environment variables
    - \c process.env in JavaScript and TypeScript programs reads and changes the process environment under
      %Qore's environment lock, as %Qore code does; Node.js used a lock of its own, so a variable that %Qore code
      changed in another thread while JavaScript code read it could be read after it was freed (on Alpine Linux
      (musl), which frees the value that \c setenv() replaces, the process could crash), and a change made by
      JavaScript code could do the same to %Qore code reading the environment or starting a process.
      \c process.env behaves as before, except that <tt>structuredClone(process.env)</tt> raises
      \c DataCloneError; clone a copy instead (<tt>structuredClone({...process.env})</tt>)
    - a @ref V8::TypeScriptProgram "TypeScriptProgram" no longer prints "ExperimentalWarning: stripTypeScriptTypes is
      an experimental feature and might change at any time" on stderr: experimental feature warnings are not printed
      unless \c NODE_OPTIONS enables warnings (\c --warnings or \c --trace-warnings); listeners of the
      \c warning event still receive them, and other warnings are printed as before
    - added @ref V8::JavaScriptProgram::getEnvironment() "JavaScriptProgram::getEnvironment()", which returns the
      variables of the process environment as they are now, read atomically, with the changes made since the process
      started; the \c ENV hash is the environment of the process when it started
    - a \c ts-proxy child process gets the environment of its parent as it is when the child is started; it got the
      environment of the parent when the parent started, so variables set or removed with \c setenv() and
      \c unsetenv() since then were missing in the child, or still set.  The environment variables that the
      TypeScript action interface reads (\c QORE_V8_CACHE_DIR, \c QORE_V8_DISABLE_CACHE, \c TS_PROXY_LOGDIR,
      \c QORE_TYPESCRIPT_ACTION_VERBOSE and \c QORE_TYPESCRIPT_ACTION_TEST_SCRIPTS) are also read from the current
      environment
    - the Google Sheets \c find_spreadsheet_rows action takes a \c header_row option, the row of the column headers
      for sheets with titles or notes above the table (rows are read and searched below it), a \c value_render
      option, to return and search the values as stored (the default), as the sheet displays them, or the formulas
      of formula cells, and a \c date_render option, to return dates as serial numbers (the default) or as the sheet
      displays them
    - fixed the Google Sheets \c find_spreadsheet_rows action leaving out the last column of every row and
      searching the column before the one named by the \c header search option (the first column was searched
      correctly only by chance); the \c new_spreadsheet_row trigger also left out the last column and read at most
      26 columns
    - fixed Google Sheets ranges for sheet titles with spaces, punctuation or quotes in the \c find_spreadsheet_rows
      action, which the API rejects unless the title is quoted
    - the Pipedrive app requests only the OAuth2 scopes its actions, record operations and triggers use;
      \c mail:full, \c recents:read, \c phone-integration and \c goals:read are no longer requested
    - accept the reviewed Pipedrive schema revision that documents the \c limit bounds (1 to 500) of the v2 list
      operations, which the catalogue's client already enforces; retain the previous compatible revisions and
      refresh CI's exact v2 source and bundle checksums
    - accept the reviewed Pipedrive schema revision of 2026-10-11: the \c ids of the v2 activity, deal,
      organization and person list operations are integers, as the records' ids are; the \c sort of the v1 lead list
      accepts every field that it documents, including \c label_ids, \c value, \c source_name, \c visible_to and
      custom fields, instead of nine enumerated ones; and the deal of a note is declared as an object directly, with
      the same nullable title; retain the previous compatible revisions and refresh CI's exact source and bundle
      checksums
    - added local HubSpot generic-call coverage for error status policies, percent-encoded contact email
      paths, and JSON array membership bodies; these behaviors require the corresponding shared
      %Qore RestClientDataProvider fix, and retain HubSpot CMS authorization checks
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qorus/issues/626">qorus issue 626</a>)
    - accept the reviewed Pipedrive schema revision adding optional, nullable \c archive_reason to lead
      updates and responses; retain the previous compatible revision and refresh CI's exact source checksums
    - an unhandled promise rejection no longer ends a JavaScript program: it is reported as a Node.js
      \c UnhandledPromiseRejectionWarning, with the rejection's stack, on standard error, and the program stays
      usable.  Before, Node's default raised it as an uncaught exception, which ended the program's environment and
      left the program unusable for good ("has been destroyed") until the host process was restarted; a single
      background request that failed with nobody waiting for it (for example a network write that timed out) disabled
      every TypeScript app sharing the program.  A program's own \c unhandledRejection handlers still run
    - preserve the embedding process's signal handlers and signal mask during Node initialization; this fixes
      broken %Qore signal delivery and crashes when Node's WebAssembly trap handler replaced the JVM's handler
    - added TypeScript compiler package support for Node.js builds without the built-in compiler, including
      Debian and Ubuntu; syntax errors are reported before execution
    - added Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the native bridge, helper modules, tools, metadata and translations
    - fixed a deadlock that hung the calling thread when a JavaScript program was destroyed while a call was in
      progress in another thread; destruction is deferred until the call in progress completes, but the deferred
      destructor was run with the (non-recursive) program lock held, and it acquires the same lock, so the thread
      finishing the call deadlocked against itself; the deferred destructor now runs with the lock released
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5383">qore issue 5383</a>)
    - fixed a race in module shutdown, where the set of JavaScript programs was iterated without holding the lock
      protecting it, while other threads could insert and erase entries concurrently
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5383">qore issue 5383</a>)
    - V8 and node are no longer torn down at module shutdown when JavaScript code is still being executed in
      another thread; disposing of the isolate and the platform under running code crashes the process, so the
      platform is intentionally leaked instead, as the process is terminating in any case
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5383">qore issue 5383</a>)
    - fixed a deadlock that could hang the process (most visibly during shutdown) when apps were initialized
      concurrently: on-demand app initialization holds an internal lock while lazily loading modules (REST schema
      validators, the app's own module, etc.), and a concurrent module load could, from its initializer, register
      an app child data provider and re-enter app initialization &mdash; the two lock orders formed an ABBA
      deadlock; app initialization now acquires the global module-load lock before its own lock (via
      @ref Qore::call_with_module_load_lock() "call_with_module_load_lock()"), giving a single consistent lock
      order (requires %Qore 3.0)
    - fixed ~15s of fixed latency per app action against upstreams that keep the HTTP connection open after the
      response (ex: Slack, YouTube / Google APIs); the embedded Node event loop was pumped with \c UV_RUN_DEFAULT,
      which over-runs until no active handles remain, so a lingering keep-alive socket stalled delivery until it
      idled out even though the response had already arrived; the loop is now pumped with \c UV_RUN_ONCE while
      waiting on a Promise and \c UV_RUN_NOWAIT for best-effort drains
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qorus/issues/343">qorus issue 343</a>)
    - added the @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::JavaScriptInProcessPool "JavaScriptInProcessPool" class for
      concurrent in-process JavaScript execution without IPC overhead
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-v8/issues/225">issue 225</a>)
    - added @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::InProcessProgramInfo "InProcessProgramInfo" hashdecl
    - added on-demand pool creation via
      @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::TypeScriptActionInterface::startInProcessServerOnDemand()
      "TypeScriptActionInterface::startInProcessServerOnDemand()" with configurable maximum pool size
    - added direct pool injection via
      @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::TypeScriptActionInterface::setInProcessServer()
      "TypeScriptActionInterface::setInProcessServer()"
    - added clone-mode closure capture mechanism using thread-local
      \c PoolCloneModeHelper to create
      pool programs without modifying global state

    @section v8_2_1 v8 Module Version 2.1
    - added the @ref V8::TypeScriptProgram "TypeScriptProgram" class for runtime TypeScript transpilation and
      execution using Node.js's built-in \c stripTypeScriptTypes() API
    - supports type stripping, interfaces, enums (including const enums), typed classes with inheritance,
      generics, namespaces, and all standard TypeScript syntax
    - TypeScript programs inherit all @ref V8::JavaScriptProgram "JavaScriptProgram" methods and the
      \c qore global object for %Qore API access
    - fixed a memory leak in \c QoreV8ProgramData::deref() where tracked V8 resources were not cleaned up
      when a constructor failed

    @section v8_2_0 v8 Module Version 2.0
    - added the \c qore global object for transparent access to %Qore APIs from JavaScript
    - JavaScript code can now access %Qore namespaces, classes, functions, constants, and enums
    - class wrapping supports constructors, instance methods, static methods, and inheritance
    - public data members of wrapped %Qore objects can be read, written, and enumerated from JavaScript
    - %Qore exceptions propagate as catchable JavaScript errors

    @section v8_1_0_4 v8 Module Version 1.0.4
    - improved ts-proxy restart robustness and shutdown handling to avoid deadlocks
    - handled EPIPE and closed sockets more gracefully in ts-proxy communications

    @section v8_1_0_3 v8 Module Version 1.0.3
    - fixed a bug returning action option info for Swagger-based actions
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4956">issue 4956</a>)

    @section v8_1_0_2 v8 Module Version 1.0.2
    - fixed a bug returning reference data in action providers
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4955">issue 4955</a>)

    @section v8_1_0_1 v8 Module Version 1.0.1
    - fixed a bug retrieving dynamic types in the \c ts-proxy process
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4938">issue 4938</a>)

    @section v8_1_0 v8 Module Version 1.0
    - initial release
*/
